How confident are you about your playing abilities?  Have you ascended
before?  Often?

If you're that afraid of messing it up, maybe get a "oLS

In any case, I'd certainly get a +oChM if you don't have one already;
once you can cast it consistently, and if you use it wisely, it can
make you nearly invincible.  BUT, see the part where I say you should
actually get a magic marker instead :) before you wish for this!

Depending on your carrying situation, you might consider a BoH; wizards
are weaklings and end up carrying all those heavy spellbooks around...

If you're looking for somewhat longer-term equipment, you could get a
Helm of Brilliance (my advice is to go for +2 not +3, since +2 will
help you quite a bit but if you go for +3 and don't get it then you
basically wasted a wish, until you get the chance to enchant it
better).

A MAGIC MARKER!!!!!  These things are awesome, and wizards are
especially sick with them too.  If you've got a lot of armor
(especially armor that you plan to keep for a while) that needs
enchanting you can write the scrolls yourself and get your AC way down.
 And also, if your luck's good enough, you can write spellbooks
yourself!  I would probably get one and write spellbooks of Charm
Monster, ID, and maybe Create Monster (awesome for sacrifice-athalons
if you can find a suitable altar).  For future reference, it's usually
cheaper in wishes to wish for a magic marker right away, and then write
the charging scroll with it, although that requires luck and holy water
(both of which are acquirable at your nearest non-guarded altar).

Hope this helps!

